- Pattern per page: sections -> get --section 0 --strip for infobox (reqs/coords) -> targeted get on Gameplay/Rewards/Requirements sections. Several pages nest their real reward tables one level deeper than the top "Rewards" H2 (e.g. Tithe Farm's "Reward shop" H3, Soul Wars' separate "Soul Wars Reward Shop" page, Shades of Mort'ton's chest-unlocking/uniques subsections) -- fetched those explicitly rather than trusting the top-level Rewards section alone.
- Found and logged the quest/minigame page-title collision for Shades of Mort'ton (see gotchas.log) -- would have silently produced a wrong-page contribution if not caught by the Otheruses hatnote in the quest page's section 0.
- Reward economies are heavily non-GE by design for several of these (pieces of eight, Castle wars tickets, Brimhaven vouchers, Zeal Tokens, reward points) -- captured item names without coin values per the never-GE discipline; this is a real design fact, not a data gap.
- No contribute failures; all 14 `contribute --file` calls returned "contributed:" on first try. 1 feedback filed (quest/minigame title-collision UX), 3 gotchas filed.
Canonical-trigger mint: when a batch brief lists items in loosely-normalized form (e.g. "Trawler" alongside "Fishing Trawler", "Shades of Morton" for "Shades of Mort'ton"), grep contrib.jsonl AND cross-check the wiki's own title via a quick `search`/Otheruses hatnote before assuming two brief-list entries are two distinct targets -- collapsing false-duplicates up front is cheaper than discovering it mid-fetch.
## minigames-3 retro
- Pre-check against contrib.jsonl (grep "key": "minigamedb:) found 25 existing rows including barbarian-assault, mahogany-homes, tempoross from the brief's "(if not done)" list -- skipped all 3 per instruction, cutting the batch from 15 to 12 real targets.
- 12/12 contributed clean: chambers-of-xeric, theatre-of-blood, tombs-of-amascut, fight-caves, inferno, fortis-colosseum, gauntlet, corrupted-gauntlet, zalcano, giants-foundry, shooting-stars, champions-challenge.
- Fetch pattern per target: sections first, then get --section N --strip on lead(0)/Transportation/Rewards (2-4 gets/page, ~9-15 total across the batch); Gauntlet needed 7 gets since Normal+Corrupted share one article across 5 non-contiguous sections.
- Three raids (CoX/ToB/ToA) turned out to have a real reqs asymmetry worth flagging for downstream chain synthesis: ToB's only hard gate is a quest (Priest in Peril), ToA's is a quest (Beneath Cursed Sands), but CoX has NO quest or level gate at all -- lowest floor of the three despite being the first raid released.
- One extra fetch needed beyond the brief's page list: "Ancient chest" (CoX's linked reward-table subpage) to get real unique-item names/rarities, since CoX's own Rewards section doesn't inline them unlike ToB/ToA -- logged as a gotcha + fed back as a CLI suggestion (get --resolve-main).
- No blocking gotchas; all targets had clean, singular canonical titles except Gauntlet/Corrupted Gauntlet (one shared article, contributed as two rows per brief) and Zalcano's level gate (buried in lead prose, no Requirements H2).
- Canonical-trigger mint: the directive should have said up front "when a brief lists two named variants of one activity (e.g. Gauntlet + Corrupted Gauntlet), expect a single shared wiki article rather than two pages, and contribute two rows against one ref" -- without that framing, a search for a standalone "Corrupted Gauntlet" article wastes a round trip on a leaderboard-only page before the shared-article structure becomes obvious.

## gear-3 retro
- Scope: 16 GEAR/EQUIPMENT progression unlocks (Abyssal whip, Dragon scimitar, Rune crossbow, Magic shortbow, Trident of the seas, Occult necklace, Berserker ring, Dragon boots, Bandos chestplate, Armadyl crossbow, Toxic blowpipe, Twisted bow, Scythe of vitur, Ancient spellbook, Lunar spellbook, Arceuus spellbook). 16/16 contributed as unlockdb:<slug>, 0 skipped -- none pre-existed (confirmed via grep of the full unlockdb: key list before starting; the unlocks-key/unlocks-2 passes had covered jewellery/travel/outfit unlocks but zero weapon/armour/spellbook items overlapped this list).
- Pattern per weapon/armour: item page section 0 (lead, states wield-level + often the source) + Creation section when fletchable/craftable (rune crossbow, magic shortbow, toxic blowpipe) + the DROP-SOURCE MONSTER's own section-0 infobox when the item's lead doesn't carry the full farming gate (Abyssal demon for the whip's 85 Slayer, Kraken for the trident's 87 Slayer+task, Smoke devil for the necklace's 93 Slayer+task, Dagannoth Rex + Waterbirth Island Dungeon for the ring, Zulrah + Tanzanite fang for the blowpipe's Regicide gate). Two raid-unique items (Twisted bow, Scythe of vitur) needed the raid's own page instead of a monster page -- confirmed neither Chambers of Xeric nor Theatre of Blood states a level requirement to attempt the raid itself, only ToB's Priest in Peril (Morytania access).
- Reuse win: all 3 spellbooks' quest gates (Desert Treasure I, Lunar Diplomacy, A Kingdom Divided) were already fully flattened under questdb:* from earlier passes -- these rows only needed the spellbook page itself (own effect/grant description) plus a pointer back to the existing questdb: row rather than re-deriving the quest chain, and Arceuus turned out to need NEITHER (talking to Tyss has zero skill/quest/item gate at all, confirmed from the page's own text -- only the expanded A Kingdom Divided spell set is quest-gated).
- Hit a real template-rendering wall: item pages' "Item sources"/"Shop locations" H2s are almost universally bare {{Drop sources|X}}/{{Store locations list|X}} template calls that don't expand through get --strip (Lua/DPL-driven) -- 5 of 16 items needed a monster-page detour because of this, and Dragon boots' exact source monster stayed unresolved ("??") after checking 3 plausible dragon-tier monsters plus the general Rare drop table's own drop lines and finding it in none of them. Logged as a gotcha rather than guessing from memory.
- anchor_hint split: 8 hard (dragon-scimitar, bandos-chestplate, armadyl-crossbow, toxic-blowpipe, twisted-bow, scythe-of-vitur, ancient-spellbook -- all big single-gate or raid-tier power spikes with real downstream training-route implications) vs 8 soft (abyssal-whip, rune-crossbow, magic-shortbow, trident-of-the-seas, occult-necklace, berserker-ring, dragon-boots, lunar-spellbook, arceuus-spellbook -- earlier/side-grade/utility unlocks). No "inline" rows this batch, unlike unlocks-key's kharedsts-memoirs case -- every target here has its own dedicated drop/craft/raid-roll action distinct from any single quest reward.
- No contribute failures; all 16 `contribute --file` calls returned "contributed:" on first try. 1 feedback filed (template-render gap), 3 gotchas filed (template-render gap, monster-side slaylvl check, raid-unique no-level-gate pattern).
Canonical-trigger mint: for any future item/gear-unlock pass, "fetch the item's Item sources/Shop locations H2" should NOT be the default move -- those sections are template stubs that render empty via this CLI. The reliable order is: item lead paragraph first (usually names the source directly), then the drop-source MONSTER's own page (its Drops subsections use {{DropsLine}} which does render) only if the lead is silent, and accept "??" rather than guessing from memory when neither surfaces a hit (as happened for Dragon boots here).

## normalize-arch retro
- Design-only pass: audited 4 prose surfaces (quest detail walls, train-* sloppy details, catalog notes blobs, cond-badge-only prereqs) and shipped NORMALIZATION.md + normalization_tasks.jsonl (93 tasks / 3 tracks: 19 FIX card-facts, 20 GENERATE skill-methods, 54 GENERATE quest-subchecklists).
- Core reuse win: quest sub-checklists need ZERO new planner concepts -- enrich.py's existing coarse_expansions machinery (_inject_coarse_atoms + _build_checkpoint_index + registry-stable chkpt ids) takes quest_expansions.jsonl/steps_quest_atoms.jsonl as sibling inputs; the GRANULARITY 17-verb atom grammar and checkpoint model transfer verbatim.
- Cordoning approach: agents contribute keyed rows only (questatoms:/methods:/cardfacts:), never write data files; the consolidator mints atom ids (q-<slug>-NN-<verb>-<target>), so no agent needs global id knowledge -- the exact failure the [consolidate] chkpt-id gotcha documented.
- FIX/GENERATE split fell out cleanly by fetch budget: card facts are a zero-fetch restructure of held prose (quest_db notes/items + contrib notes); methods[] and quest atoms need wiki-grounded new data, but the 1,546-entry manifest cache makes most gets free.
- Every micro_prompt is fully interpolated (0.8-1.3k tokens): scope ids, exact page titles, one verbatim grep for held rows, output schema + key, inherited trap list (Quick-guide stubs, title redirects, coord envelope, section-suffixed slugs) -- built to kill the 80k-tokens-for-2k-of-work failure mode.
- Flagged but deferred: all web/plugin render work (sub-checklist render, reqs/rewards/start blocks, methods picker) -- WebFragments.java has a concurrent edit in flight; follow-on tasks must rebase on it.
Canonical-trigger mint: before designing normalization for any derived surface (catalog.jsonl, route fixtures), diff the derived rows against their SOURCE rows first -- here quest_db already held start/length/structured reqs that the catalog builder was dropping, so a chunk of the "missing structure" was a one-line builder fix, not fan-out research; scoping research before checking the builder would have re-fetched data the repo already held.
